{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home/mission — why this exists, and what it does for you.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     This band replaces the testimonial section in NSDS's homepage archetype,
     and that is a deliberate swap rather than a gap. A testimonial is
     borrowed credibility, and a site with no learners yet has none to borrow
     — a quote invented to fill the slot is the one thing on a homepage that
     can actively cost trust. What a new project HAS is a reason for existing,
     so that is what goes in the slot.

     Three cards, and the order is an argument: the problem, the position
     taken on it, and what the reader gets. .ns-features is NSDS's own
     three-up. .ns-feature__top is a ROW holding the glyph and the mono index
     — the index is NSDS's second motif, a first-class element rather than a
     hidden label, so it is markup here and not a ::before.

     ── THE HEAD IS LEFT-ALIGNED, AND IT IS THE ONLY BAND THAT CHANGED ───────
     .ns-band__head--center has been dropped. .ns-band__head is capped at
     --container-narrow (56rem), so centred it floated as an island with the
     three cards below starting at a different left edge; left-aligned, the
     kicker, the heading, the lede and card 01 all begin on the same line the
     hero's headline began on. With the bar now contained to the same 72rem,
     that is ONE left edge from the brand mark down to here.

     home/follow and home/marquee still centre their heads. That is not an
     oversight — they are both short, single-idea bands with nothing beneath
     them to align to, so there is no edge for them to break. If the page
     ever reads as inconsistent, those two are the ones to revisit.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <header class="ns-band__head">
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Why this exists"}}</span>
            <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Salesforce is not hard. Learning it is."}}</h2>
            <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "The documentation is complete, the videos are endless, and neither tells you what to learn next. That gap is the whole problem."}}</p>
        </header>

        <div class="ns-features">
            <div class="ns-feature">
                <div class="ns-feature__top">{{> "icons/compass"}}<span class="ns-feature__num">01</span></div>
                <h3 class="ns-feature__name">{{t "The mission"}}</h3>
                <p class="ns-feature__text">{{t "One ordered path from your first org to code you can defend in review — so that at every point you know exactly what comes next, and why."}}</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ns-feature">
                <div class="ns-feature__top">{{> "icons/flask"}}<span class="ns-feature__num">02</span></div>
                <h3 class="ns-feature__name">{{t "How it is taught"}}</h3>
                <p class="ns-feature__text">{{t "Plain English first, then a concrete example you build in a free Developer Edition org, then the bridge to the next lesson. No filler, no intro music."}}</p>
            </div>

            <div class="ns-feature">
                <div class="ns-feature__top">{{> "icons/users-three"}}<span class="ns-feature__num">03</span></div>
                <h3 class="ns-feature__name">{{t "How you can help"}}</h3>
                <p class="ns-feature__text">{{t "It is being written in the open. Tell me what to cover next, correct what is wrong, or star the repo — the theme and the design system are both MIT."}}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
